cies","target":"ca-policies","line":124},{"title":"Email","target":"email","line":125},{"title":"Logs","target":"logs","line":126}],"metadata":{"title":"Domain separation explained","description":"With domain separation, you can segregate application data, UI, and business logic, such as rules or workflows, in a single customer instance. Separating these elements into logically defined domains supports specific hierarchies for all customers using your applications.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/platform-security/bp-what-is-domain-separation.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":7,"breadcrumb":["Recommended practices for service providers","Domain separation for service providers","Access Management"],"tags":["#platform-security","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/platform-security/bp-what-is-domain-separation.md"},
